{
  "name": "Daily Ecom Briefing",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this does\n\nRuns at 7am. Pulls yesterday from **three systems that do not agree with each\nother**, works out which number is the truth, and writes the CEO a short note in\nplain English.\n\nTwo days are pinned here. **One reconciles and sends. One does not, and is held\nfor a person instead** - because a briefing built on numbers nobody has checked\nis worse than no briefing.\n\nNo dashboard. The CEO does not want to log into anything at 7am; they want to\nknow whether yesterday was fine.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1900,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Shopify and the books will never match\n\nThis is the part every dashboard project gets wrong, and it is the whole reason\nthis workflow exists.\n\nShopify says **$15,405**. QuickBooks says **$15,155**. Both are right.\n\nThe $250 difference is a **gift card**. Redeeming a gift card is not new\nrevenue - the money was already booked on the day the card was *sold*. Counting\nit again would be counting it twice. So the two systems disagree, and the\ndisagreement is **correct**.\n\nRefunds, tax, shipping, discounts and the timezone the day is cut on all do the\nsame thing. A CEO dashboard that shows three numbers for \"sales yesterday\" is\ndead inside a week, and no amount of AI on top of it fixes that.\n\n**So the system picks a number of record - the books - explains every dollar of\nthe difference, and refuses to publish anything it cannot explain.**\n\nThe second day is that refusal: a $1,560 gap with nothing to account for it.\nIt does not guess, and it does not quietly average. It asks Finance.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "c4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1430,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Two things worth saying on the call\n\n**Meta's revenue number is a claim, not an accounting fact.** The platform is\nmarking its own homework - it counts a sale as its own if the buyer saw an ad\nwithin the attribution window, and Klaviyo will claim the same sale on the same\nday. Add every channel's attributed revenue together and you get more revenue\nthan the business actually made. So ROAS here is **blended**: real money in,\ndivided by real money out. Meta's figure is shown, and labelled as Meta's.\n\n**Everything that sends is greyed out** - the CEO email, the Finance alert, and\nthe history log. It runs end to end and leaves nothing behind.\n\n**The AI never sees an unreconciled number.** It writes about figures that have\nalready been agreed by the arithmetic upstream. That ordering is the design.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "c4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -890,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 7 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "c4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Every Morning at 7am",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -1880,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
